# minus 1 in triple-double (|expm1(x)| ≥ 0.0155: at most 6.1 bits of cancellation; measured 2^-152); for
# E ≥ 120 the −1 is below 2^-114 of e^x, inside exp's own worst-case distance (Lefèvre–Muller: 2^-113 for
# |x| ≥ 2^-30), so it cannot move the rounding and expm1 rounds as exp does.
